id: pm-hke9z7
title: "MCP read tools silently ignore declared flat parameters: pm_context reads none, and for/tokenBudget/depth on pm_list, pm_search, pm_next and pm_get never reach the intent layer"
description: "Discovered while verifying pm-gh1644 over MCP (published 2026.10.31 and current source both reproduce).\n\nEvery narrow MCP read tool declares its action parameters flat in its inputSchema (pm_context declares for, limit, depth, section, fields, tokenBudget, ...; pm_list/pm_search/pm_next/pm_get declare for and tokenBudget). The SDK runtime only moves a flat argument into the options record the handlers read when it appears in the hand-maintained HOISTED_ACTION_OPTION_KEYS table in src/sdk/runtime-input.ts. That table has no context entry at all and omits for/tokenBudget (and most filters) from list, search, next and get. A flat argument outside the table is accepted without a warning (it is declared) and then dropped.\n\nMeasured in a fresh sandbox through the MCP tools/call handler, flat vs nested options: pm_context {depth: deep} → depth brief (nested → deep); pm_context {for: orient, limit: 10} → no intent, limit null, token_budget 1600 (nested → orient, limit 3); pm_list {for: triage}, pm_search {query, for: discover}, pm_next {for: execute}, pm_get {id, for: inspect} → no context_intent receipt (nested → applied); pm_next {limit: 1} → 5 rows (nested → 1). The declared intent layer is therefore unreachable for MCP hosts that send the flat arguments the schema advertises. Same defect family as pm-wcaa (pm_files declared-but-ignored params, closed individually) and pm-hno5.\n\nDuplicate search: 'MCP pm_context flat arguments ignored options', 'MCP declared parameter silently ignored', 'mcp for intent not applied' — no open item."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: agent-ux,context,contracts,mcp
created_at: "2026-10-31T21:27:47.547Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-31T22:31:37.663Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-31T22:31:35.081Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-31T22:31:35.081Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "For context, get, list, next and search, every optional parameter the action's tool contract declares is hoisted from flat MCP arguments into the handler options (derived from PM_TOOL_ACTION_PARAMETER_CONTRACTS, not a hand list), nested options still win; flat and nested calls produce identical results for for, limit, depth and tokenBudget on all five tools; a regression test iterates every declared optional key of the five actions and fails if one is not hoisted"
parent: pm-5k4v
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "runtime-input.ts derives flat-to-options hoisting for context, get, list, next and search from PM_TOOL_ACTION_PARAMETER_CONTRACTS[action].optional, excluding the query/keywords operands. One hoisted-key list replaces three loops, and nested options still win. runMcpSearchAction reads query, then the declared keywords alias, then refuses with the unchanged missing-query error."
expected_result: "An MCP host that sends the flat parameters a read tool's schema declares gets the same intent, projection and limits as the nested options form."
actual_result: "Through the MCP tools/call handler, flat and nested now agree for pm_context depth/for/limit, for on pm_list/pm_search/pm_next/pm_get, pm_get depth and pm_next limit. The flat orient call also discloses the limit override. read-tool-flat-parameters spec 7/7 iterates every declared optional key; 6/7 fail with the fix stashed. mcp-handshake hoist expectations pass."
